{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 413 days after the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D3"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows ibutilide fumarate has been listed since 2022-04-29 and as of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on the list for 54 months.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label identifies Pharmacia & Upjohn Company LLC (FEI 1810189) as the registered plant for manufacture, analysis, API manufacture, labeling, and packing.",
      "cites": ["E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1208260 at that plant ended 2023-06-16 and was classified VAI, with the classification letter dated 2024-09-10 — 413 days after the shortage posting on 2022-04-29.",
      "cites": ["D3", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier FDA inspections at the same plant (564470, 682230, 746375, 796422, 837169, 933762, 1066512) were also classified VAI between 2009 and 2018.",
      "cites": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E6", "E7", "E8", "E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 54 vials (0.1 mg/mL, 10 mL) with 4.5 vials used per day, giving 11.9 days on hand; Corvale Lakeside holds 12 vials at 1 vial per day, giving 12.3 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to buy from Heritage Pharmaceuticals Inc. d/b/a Avet Pharmaceuticals Inc., which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    }
  ]
}
